            <ArticleTitle>Bilateral Hypoplasia of the Medial and Lateral Menisci.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>150-152</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.5792/ksrr.15.070</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Hypoplasia of the meniscus is a very rare congenital abnormality, with only a few cases reported to date. A 9-year-old girl visited our hospital due to lateral knee pain following a hyperextension injury to the left knee. Magnetic resonance imaging showed hypoplasia of the medial and lateral menisci, as well as a posterior horn tear of the lateral meniscus, in both knee joints. To our knowledge, this is the first report of a patient with hypoplasia of the medial and lateral menisci in both knee joints.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
